{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["And <b>the Rock, His deed is perfect</b> begins, to make known that all that befell Israel was on account of their evil deeds." "The meaning of <b>the Rock.</b> That He stands always like a rock (צור). Do not wonder, for thus Scripture says, \"like a lion (כארי) he roars\" — for speech is unable to compare the deeds of HaShem, may He be exalted, except to His own deeds, for all is His deed. And likewise \"the rock of my heart (צור לבבי)\" — like a support and strength and standing. And some say from the language of form (צורה), and likewise \"their rock (וצורם) consumes to Sheol.\" And the essence: He has no substance that receives; rather He is the Primeval Rock. And the first interpretation is correct in my eyes." "<b>His deed is perfect.</b> For every agent's product is deficient, because it needs that which is above it — except the product of the honored HaShem, and all [differ] (some read שונים) except the Former of all. The [text] in MS 48 reads שונים." "<b>For all His ways are justice.</b> That they do not change; rather they are upon one justice. And this is the praise (some read התחלה) — and all created beings' deeds change according to their needs, but the deeds of HaShem (some read לבדו) are in might according to wisdom. And one should not raise an objection from the sun standing still, for its secret is clear in the word \"and the moon (בעמק אילון)\", as I explained in its place." "<b>El of faithfulness and without injustice.</b> He alone has true might, for every might among the mighty is an accident from another's hand. And the meaning: after He is El of faithfulness, it is impossible that He do injustice, and it is possible that \"and without injustice\" refers to His ways. Or the word El draws itself and another with it." "<b>Righteous and upright is He.</b> Because He said \"they have corrupted (שחת) to Him,\" He says that their corruption is with crookedness, but He alone is upright, and uprightness straightens the crooked; therefore \"to Him,\" because they were His at the beginning."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 32, :notes {1 "Ibn Ezra cites Hosea 11:10; 'כארי' is Hosea's phrasing, not the MT reading 'כארי' at that verse.", 2 "The base text reads 'שנים'; a variant in MS 48 reads 'שונים' (differ). The syntax of the parenthesis recording the MS variant is rendered literally and is difficult.", 3 "Two parenthetical variant readings appear in the text: התחלה for התהלה, and לבדו for לכבודו. The reference to 'the sun standing still' is Joshua 10:12-13."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:25:56.200632427Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}